          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SemiLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SemiLat
            be the category of meet-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattices"} semilattices
            (i.e.,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            admitting finite meets); equivalently, the category of idempotent commutative monoids. Regarding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpinski space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = \{0 \leq 1\}
            ambimorphically either as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            or as a meet-semilattice, i.e., an internal idempotent commutative monoid in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            seen as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} dualizing object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            given by homming into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                  %msup
                    %mi SemiLat
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi SemiLat
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi SemiLat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Top
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top \stackrel{Top(-, \mathbf{2})^{op}}{\to} SemiLat^{op} \;\; \dashv \;\; SemiLat^{op} \stackrel{SemiLat(-, \mathbf{2})}{\to} Top.
          %p
            In more detail: for a space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{2}
            is naturally identified with the set of open subsets, i.e., the topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            (where the pointwise meet-semilattice structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(X, \mathbf{2})
            coincides with the meets defined by intersection on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SemiLat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SemiLat(L, \mathbf{2})
            is topologized as a subspace of the product space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^{{|L|}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|L|}
            copies of Sierpinski space. The adjunction says that there is a natural bijection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo →
                      %mi Top
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi SemiLat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{L \to Top(X, \mathbf{2})}{X \to SemiLat(L, \mathbf{2})}
          %p between semilattice maps above and continuous maps below.
          %p
            The
            %strong filter monad
            is the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Filt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Filt
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            induced by this adjunction. (Compare
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter+monad"} ultrafilter monad
          %p
            For a space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Filt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Filt(X)
            is the set of meet-preserving maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X) \to \mathbf{2}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            that are upward-closed and closed under finite intersections, i.e.,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filters"} filters
            in
            = succeed "." do
